  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nThe pattern through the extended will feature a broad upper\nlevel ridge extending across the central CONUS while a deep\ntrough becomes established off the Pacific Northwest coast. The\nridge and southwesterly flow aloft through the period will push\ntemperatures to around 10 degrees above normal, with valley \nhighs generally reaching the 60s. Breezy southeast winds will \ndevelop over the weekend as a system clips the Pacific \nNorthwest. However, precipitation will remain north of our area \nwith only periods of high clouds. Dry conditions will persist \ninto early next week, but a 10-30% chance of precipitation and \nbreezy conditions will return on Wednesday as a strong system \napproaches the coast.",
